_pdbx_entry_details.entry_id                   1EA5 
_pdbx_entry_details.compound_details           
;HYDROLYZES CHOLINE RELEASED INTO THE SYNAPSE.
 CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ACETYLCHOLINE + H(2)O = CHOLINE + ACETATE.
 INHIBITORS OF THE ENZYME ACETYLCHOLINESTERASE (ACHE) SLOW AND
 SOMETIMES REVERSE THE COGNITIVE DECLINE EXPERIENCED BY INDIVIDUALS
 WITH ALZHEIMER'S DISEASE.
 TORPEDO CALIFONICA ACETYLCHOLINESTERASE IS A G2 DIMER IN
 SOLUTION (SEE SUSSMAN 1988). THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT CONTAINS A
 MONOMER, WITH THE CRYSTALLOGRAPHIC TWO-FOLD AXIS RELATING
 THE TWO MONOMERS IN A DIMER.
 THIS IS THE HIGHEST RESOLUTION ACETYLCHLINESTERASE
 DETERMINED SO FAR.
 THERE IS RECENT EVIDENCE (SEE BUCHT 1996) THAT THE GPI
 ANCHOR IS ATTACHED TO EITHER SER 543 OR SER 544, NOT TO CYS
 537.
;
